            <title><![CDATA[News Wrap: Blanche nomination clears Senate Judiciary Committee]]></title>
            <link>https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/news-wrap-blanche-nomination-clears-senate-judiciary-committee</link>
            <description><![CDATA[In our news wrap Tuesday, acting Attorney General Todd Blanche is a step closer to securing the job permanently after the Senate Judiciary Committee narrowly approved his nomination, civil rights groups are demanding answers after a man from El Salvador died in ICE custody and Iran and Oman are reportedly nearing a potential deal that would reopen the Strait of Hormuz.]]></description>
